AB  - Natural disasters pose significant threats to human life, infrastructure, and the environment, necessitating the development of intelligent and proactive disaster management systems. This chapter presents a novel AIOps-enabled IoT framework designed for early warning, risk assessment, and automated response in natural disaster scenarios such as floods, earthquakes, wildfires, and cyclones. The proposed framework integrates multi-source IoT sensor data with Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps) to enable real-time monitoring, anomaly detection, predictive analytics, and automated decision-making. The system architecture comprises four core layers: the sensing layer for environmental data collection, the edge-fog-cloud integration layer for scalable data handling, the AIOps layer for deep learning-based analytics and alert generation, and the response layer for coordinated emergency action. Advanced machine learning models including CNN-LSTM for spatiotemporal forecasting and GNNs for topological event prediction are employed. Additionally, automated root cause analysis and feedback loops enhance the system's self-healing and adaptation capabilities. Case studies using open datasets validate the system's accuracy, responsiveness, and applicability in real-world scenarios. The chapter also discusses challenges such as data privacy, deployment in low-infrastructure areas, and real-time constraints. This AIOps-IoT synergy aims to revolutionize disaster management by offering faster, smarter, and more reliable early warning mechanisms.
ER  - 

