AB  - The 5G Core (5GC) is a critical component of next-generation mobile networks, and its reliable operation increasingly relies on Artificial Intelligence for IT operations (AIOps) to detect, localize, and mitigate anomalies. These AIOps pipelines process thousands of correlated telemetry streams exported by the 5GC, where anomaly detection in multivariate time-series (MTS) metrics is challenging due to cross-metric coupling induced by shared underlying counters and derived performance measurements, non-stationarity from software updates and traffic fluctuations, and limited incident labeling. This work introduces TeleGAN-Core, a generative adversarial network (GAN) designed for one-class anomaly detection in 5GC performance metrics. Both the generator and an autoencoder-based critic are implemented using Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BiLSTM) autoencoders. The critic is trained as a reconstruction-energy model, and the resulting generator and critic reconstruction errors are combined through a weighted anomaly-scoring formulation. A 5GC-aware preprocessing pipeline standardizes heterogeneous metrics and constructs service-oriented multivariate streams for each network function and interface, enabling seamless integration into AIOps workflows. TeleGAN-Core is evaluated on production 5GC telemetry and on the public SWaT and WADI industrial multivariate time-series benchmarks using a unified experimental protocol. Across these datasets, the proposed model achieves stronger anomaly-detection performance than the evaluated recurrent, adversarial, and transformer-based baselines under the reported experimental protocol. On the 5GC telemetry, TeleGAN-Core detects most labeled anomaly episodes while maintaining a favorable balance between precision and recall under class imbalance. The results also show low detection delay at the operational aggregation scale, supporting the suitability of the proposed framework for near-real-time 5GC AIOps monitoring. These results, together with its performance on additional industrial benchmarks, suggest that combining adversarial, sequence-aware modeling with 5GC-aware preprocessing can provide an effective basis for low-latency anomaly detection in 5GC AIOps environments and related operational telemetry.
ER  - 

