AB  - The fast changes in software development techniques have made integrating security, privacy, and artificial intelligence-driven operations into a single framework necessary. This paper presents DevSec Privacy AIOps, a fresh approach combining Development (Dev), Security (Sec), Privacy, and Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps) into a coherent methodology. While addressing security issues, conventional DevSecOps techniques sometimes ignore privacy needs and lack intelligent automation capacity. Our suggested framework solves these constraints by using privacy-by-design ideas and artificial intelligence-driven operational intelligence all through the software development process. We introduce a complete approach comprising mathematical models for AIOps intelligence quotient, privacy protection efficacy, and risk assessment. Over a 12-month implementation period, the empirical evaluation shows notable gains: a 50.7% decrease in security events, a 96% improvement in privacy compliance scores, a 36.1% increase in anomaly detection accuracy, and a positive return on investment of 1612% by the second year. The framework achieves outstanding cross-functional integration with an Integration Maturity Index of 4.9 out of 5.
