AB  - Artificial Intelligence for IT operations (AIOps) arose as a suitable approach to mitigate cyberattacks, since traditional defenses are no longer sufficient. However, it is necessary to evolve AIOps to deal with emerging threats. Within this context, this article presents a solution that integrates machine learning with multi-source threat intelligence in the AIOps cycle to analyze the risk of network connections and prevent malicious IPs from accessing the network. For the evaluation, a dataset was built with real data, and multiple AI models were tested, demonstrating high accuracy and efficiency in detecting threats. Deployment in a campus gateway confirmed the solution’s feasibility in real-world conditions.
