AB  - The telecommunications sector is characterised by its intricacy, with success dependent on the efficacy of operations across multiple corporate divisions. Artificial intelligence (AI) has arisen as a viable instrument to streamline and enhance these procedures. South Africans are now starting to leverage AI's potential, especially in enhancing in-store consumer experiences, optimising call centre efficiency, and streamlining staff deployment. In a financially tough environment, investing in AI may appear formidable. Nonetheless, prominent mobile network providers have adopted AI, while emerging digital competitors are transforming the sector by utilising AI within the context of software-defined and cloud-based networks. To maintain competitiveness, South African mobile firms are aligning with advancing technology and the innovators facilitating its adoption. The telecom sector, propelled by the rapid expansion of mobile technology and 5G, has emerged as a focal point for contemporary technology, with artificial intelligence in telecoms at the forefront. Operational management is notoriously complex, frequently regarded as the most intricate aspect of the company. To excel in this domain, telecom operators must implement a synchronised and cohesive strategy across several business units, with artificial intelligence serving as an enabler in this endeavour. To this end, the sole purpose of this study was to determine and assess the driving determinants influencing the adoption of AIOPS in the South African mobile network industry and to explore the causeeffect relationship between them. From the research results of this study, it can be observed that network optimisation stands as the most significant reason for the application of AIOPS in the mobile industry Artificial intelligence is significantly influencing the telecommunications sector. It is facilitating mobile operators in enhancing connection and the user experience.
ER  - 

