AB  - The increased complexity of contemporary data pipelines with both high volume and high velocity and diverse data flows in a hybrid cloud-edge architecture necessitates an adaptable and resilient operations model. This paper will introduce the Hybrid AIOps that combines graph-based dependency intelligence and statistical anomaly detection with autonomous multi-agent coordination to provide the proactive maintenance and self-healing features in distributed data ecosystems. The suggested architecture combines both time-series analytics to detect trend deviations and graph intelligence models to represent topological dependencies among the data pipeline components to be able to localize the root-cause accurately. Moreover, an autonomous hierarchy of agents is made to use reinforcement learning and policy-based coordination to reconfigure dynamically pipeline resources to minimize downtime and maximize the quality of services. The experimental validation of simulated data workload using enterprise data has proven higher accuracy of fault-prediction by 19%, shorter mean time to recovery (MTTR) by 27% and overall improved system resilience. The paper identifies the synergies between statistical learning and graph-based reasoning as the capabilities of AIOps systems to evolve beyond the reactive monitoring to fully self-adaptive pipelines governance that is applicable to Industry 5.0 data infrastructure.
