AB  - Accurate CPU utilization forecasting is essential for intelligent operations (AIOps) in data centers, yet traditional models struggle to capture the complex, nonlinear characteristics of workloads. To address this challenge, this paper proposes an RF-Optuna-LightGBM prediction framework that integrates Random Forest (RF)-based feature selection with Bayesian hyperparameter optimization via Optuna. The framework identifies key temporal drivers from multi-scale features using RF and adaptively tunes LightGBM parameters to enhance model robustness and predictive accuracy. Experiments on real server monitoring datasets demonstrate that the proposed method outperforms baseline models—including ARIMA, LSTM, and default LightGBM—in terms of RMSE, MAE, and R2, achieving superior forecasting precision and generalization. This approach offers an effective and scalable solution for proactive AIOps in data centers.
