AB  - The escalating complexity of power information systems necessitates increasingly stringent requirements for the precision and latency of Root Cause Analysis (RCA) within Intelligent Operations and Maintenance (AIOps). Existing knowledgedriven methodologies encounter a critical dichotomy: semanticcentric retrieval models often remain topology-agnostic, precluding deep causal inference, while static graph-based paradigms lack the requisite agility to accommodate real-time system dynamics. To bridge these gaps, we propose TC-RCA, a temporal and topological-aware retrieval-augmented generation framework. Specifically, we design a hybrid topology-semantic graph to formalize deterministic dependencies, implement a dual-layer retrieval algorithm weighted by temporal-causal factors to refine evidence acquisition, and incorporate a streaming memory architecture to enable seamless incremental updates. Empirical evaluations on authentic power system datasets demonstrate that TC-RCA significantly outperforms state-of-the-art baselines in terms of response accuracy and contextual relevance, underscoring its efficacy and superiority for mission-critical industrial AIOps scenarios.
