AB  - The rapid adoption of containerized microservices on Kubernetes has intensified operational complexity for Site Reliability Engineers (SREs). Traditional threshold based monitoring tools such as Prometheus and Alertmanager are reactive by design and cannot detect latent or unknown anomalies in large scale, dynamic clusters. This paper presents KubeAIOps, a lightweight, entity centric AIOps framework that automates metric collection, anomaly detection, and root cause analysis (RCA) for Kubernetes clusters without requiring labeled training data. The framework continuously collects multi source telemetry node metrics, Kubernetes component metrics, and application metrics partitions them by entity type and identity, and stores time windowed feature vectors in Parquet files on a Persistent Volume. Per entity Isolation Forest models perform unsupervised anomaly detection every minute. Anomaly persistence tracking filters transient spikes, escalating only sustained anomalies to an LLM based RCA service. The RCA agent, powered by LangChain, correlates aggregated metric context with logs retrieved from Elasticsearch and generates human readable root cause explanations delivered via email. Periodic model retraining via Kubeflow Pipelines ensures adaptive learning as workloads evolve. KubeAIOps addresses key challenges in AIOps literature: label scarcity, cluster heterogeneity, alert fatigue, and lack of contextual intelligence.
ER  - 

