AB  - Traditional reactive maintenance strategies create significant impact on business performance. This approach often leads to unexpected and costly downtime, disrupting IT operations thereby causing server impact to business and their customers. As organizations increasingly focus on operational efficiency and reliability, there is a growing recognition of the need to shift towards more proactive maintenance strategies that can predict and prevent failures before they occur, thereby optimizing and minimizing unplanned downtime and impact on business. AIOps, or Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations, a rapidly evolving field that combines machine learning, big data analytics, and automation to enhance IT operations management, has provided the solution to this problem. In this paper, we share our experience with the use of AIOps to implement predictive maintenance in a real-world hybrid cloud environment and our findings accentuate its effectiveness.
