AB  - With the deepening advancement of educational digitalization strategies, university Teaching equipment management is transitioning from "construction-focused" to "operation-focused". This study focuses on integrating artificial intelligence (AI) with equipment full lifecycle management (PLM). Recent research progress and evolution paths of AI-empowered equipment operation management are systematically reviewed. A framework deeply integrating AI and PLM for intelligent equipment operation is proposed. This framework centers on two dimensions: the Artificial Intelligence for Operations (AIOps) and full-process control covering equipment planning, procurement, operational use, maintenance, and disposal. Practice demonstrates superior performance compared to traditional approaches and basic AI-assisted solutions. Specifically, in high-load scenarios, the proposed AIOps+PLM integration model enhances operational and maintenance efficiency by approximately 75.5% and 50.1%, respectively. Economically, a full lifecycle cost analysis on multimedia teaching equipment reveals cost reduction rates of 30.4% and 21.2% against the traditional and AI-assisted modes, respectively. Enhanced efficiency in university teaching equipment asset management and teaching quality assurance is thereby achieved.
ER  - 

