AB  - An efficient and predictive anomaly detection for computational resources is a key requirement for effective IT operations. This capability is critical for achieving robust and proactive AIOps within complex and heterogeneous environments. In this paper, we propose a Bidirectional-LSTM Autoencoder architecture for anomaly detection. The model is first pre-trained on a large-scale Microsoft Azure VM dataset and then fine-tuned on the Alibaba Cloud Trace container dataset, allowing effective transfer learning across different virtualization environments. Experimental results show that the proposed approach consistently reaches high accuracy while maintaining a small model size and inference times suitable for real-time AIOps operations. Qualitative analysis confirms the model's ability to detect anomalous patterns in an accurate way. These findings demonstrated that the proposed model is both accurate and efficient, making it suitable for cloud platforms and edge intelligence applications.
