AB  - This paper addresses the integration of large language models and multi-agent systems within the AIOps (Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations) paradigm for automating system telemetry analysis and failure root cause identification. A decomposed analysis architecture is presented, encompassing stages from basic metric collection to intelligent inference using a network of interacting AI agents. The paper examines root cause localization methods based on chain-of-thought reasoning, the application of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to mitigate hallucination risks, as well as inter-agent communication protocols and security control considerations. The emphasis is placed on overcoming the limitations of single-model approaches through task distribution among specialized agents, thereby improving diagnostic reliability and enabling the transition toward autonomous self-healing of IT infrastructures.
