AB  - Time series anomaly detection is a very important application field. Its purpose is to identify deviated samples from the normal sample distribution of the time series. Aiming at the challenges of accuracy and robustness faced by time series anomaly detection in industrial equipment monitoring, this paper proposes an innovative BiLSTM-AutoEncoder neural network model based on multi-scale feature fusion, which could, extract the features of time series data from multiple scales for anomaly detection, and combine a dual-path decoder for data decoding. Experiments on the Server Machine Dataset (SMD) show that the F1-Score of the proposed, model reaches 92.13%, significantly superior to mainstream baseline models such as iForest, OmniAnomaly, and Anomaly Transformer. It effectively solves the problems of insufficient capture of complex time series patterns and inadequate feature expression, providing an efficient and reliable anomaly detection solution for Artificial Intelligence for IT Operations (AIOps).
ER  - 

