AB  - Traditional industrial troubleshooting relies on linear, human-dependent workflows: log collection, manual analysis, and reactive remediation. This often leads to high Mean Time to Resolution (MTTR) and latency in processing large telemetry payloads. This paper proposes an Agentic AI architecture that transitions IT support from reactive “ticket resolving” to autonomous “reliability engineering.” We introduce the Guardian Agent Framework, which utilizes a Large Language Model (LLM) equipped with a Model Context Protocol (MCP) to actively investigate S3-hosted telemetry logs from enterprise servers. We validate the system's scalability through a component-level simulation, demonstrating a $\mathbf{1 0 x}$ improvement in ingestion throughput using an asynchronous claim-check pattern. Furthermore, based on established AIOps benchmarks, the framework is projected to reduce MTTR by up to 42 % while adhering to strict Responsible AI governance for automated dispatching.
ER  - 

